ehyde feed but is an inferred integrated supply route, not a demonstrated complete environmental synthesis.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_009\", \"rxn_016\", \"rxn_017\", \"rxn_015\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_016\", \"mol_023\", \"mol_022\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P7\",\n      \"name\": \"Thermal ammoniacal HCN ensemble\",\n      \"description\": \"Concentrated cyanide chemistry generates unidentified hydrolyzable precursors from which threonine has been recovered. The single reaction node explicitly lumps precursor formation and later hydrolysis; it does not assert that free threonine forms during polymer aging.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_018\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P8\",\n      \"name\": \"Ionizing-radiation cyanide ensemble\",\n      \"description\": \"Aqueous cyanide irradiation followed by hydrolysis has a direct experimental threonine endpoint. The precursor sequence is unresolved, and no natural dose rate, required accumulation time or mild environmental hydrolysis efficiency is established.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_019\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P9\",\n      \"name\": \"H2S-rich gas-water discharge ensemble\",\n      \"description\": \"Represents the threonine-positive Miller configuration with explicit reference gas partial pressures and possible electrode effects. Its natural analogue requires local reducing conditions and effective gas-water cycling; a particular molecular mechanism is not inferred from product detection.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_020\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P10\",\n      \"name\": \"Dry reducing-gas discharge and subsequent hydrolysis\",\n      \"description\": \"Separates dry energetic residue formation from later water-dependent release of threonine. Historical laboratory recovery supports accessibility, while gas maintenance, residue survival, exposure and environmentally effective hydrolysis remain open.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_021\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hub_molecules\": [\n    \"mol_001\",\n    \"mol_002\",\n    \"mol_003\",\n    \"mol_004\",\n    \"mol_005\",\n    \"mol_006\",\n    \"mol_007\",\n    \"mol_016\",\n    \"mol_019\",\n    \"mol_022\"\n  ],\n  \"convergence_points\": [\n    {\n      \"molecule_id\": \"mol_006\",\n      \"incoming_reactions\": [\"rxn_001\"],\n      \"outgoing_reactions\": [\"rxn_002\", \"rxn_003\", \"rxn_004\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"molecule_id\": \"mol_007\",\n      \"incoming_reactions\": [\"rxn_002\", \"rxn_003\", \"rxn_004\"],\n      \"outgoing_reactions\": [\"rxn_005\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"molecule_id\": \"mol_016\",\n      \"incoming_reactions\": [\"rxn_009\"],\n      \"outgoing_reactions\": [\"rxn_010\", \"rxn_016\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"molecule_id\": \"mol_022\",\n      \"incoming_reactions\": [\"rxn_014\", \"rxn_017\"],\n      \"outgoing_reactions\": [\"rxn_015\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"molecule_id\": \"mol_014\",\n      \"incoming_reactions\": [\"rxn_008\", \"rxn_012\", \"rxn_015\", \"rxn_018\", \"rxn_019\", \"rxn_020\", \"rxn_021\"],\n      \"outgoing_reactions\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"molecule_id\": \"mol_015\",\n      \"incoming_reactions\": [\"rxn_008\", \"rxn_012\", \"rxn_015\"],\n      \"outgoing_reactions\": []\n    }\n  ]\n}", "parsed_response": {"target_molecule": "Threonine", "overall_strategy": "Construct a connected terrestrial network containing 10 distinct feedstock or activation sequences. These are not 10 independently demonstrated environmental syntheses: three pathways are alternative implementations of lactaldehyde photochemistry, two converge through glycine, and four represent experimentally supported but mechanistically unresolved reaction ensembles. The strongest defined target-forming branches are aminomalononitrile plus acetaldehyde a